      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Families from New York arrived in 1805, planting the first farms along the west bank of the Chagrin River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Mayfield,_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village’s gently rolling hills belong to the Chagrin River watershed, directing small streams that feed the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Mayfield,_Ohio",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Bennett‑Van Curen House, built in 1847, stands as a well‑preserved example of 19th‑century farmstead architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Mayfield,_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mayfield Township, the area’s original administrative unit, was created on June 14, 1819, after splitting from Chagrin Township.",
